; v0.1 trial, part B: start every installed candidate once.
;     Execute PAYLOAD:R/TRIALB
; Windowed programs: Run, wait 15 s, Status records whether the process is
; alive, then Ctrl-C if it still is, and Status again. Shell tools: input from
; NIL: so none can block, output and return code to the log. Nothing is typed
; or clicked while this runs; the host only takes screenshots.
;
; The drawer is <root>/<id>, NOT the archive's own drawer name: the first run
; of this script CD'd to the archive names and five of them do not exist.
; FAILAT is high because a tool's own return code (bin2iso answers its usage
; with 20) must not end the run; the first run stopped at DiskUsage.

FAILAT 1000
Delete RAM:trialb-console.txt QUIET
Copy PAYLOAD:PUTFILE RAM:putfile
Protect RAM:putfile +e

Echo >>RAM:trialb-console.txt "*N==== screentest ===="
Date >>RAM:trialb-console.txt
CD SYS:PkgV01/screentest
Run >NIL: <NIL: ScreenTest
Wait 15
Echo >>RAM:trialb-console.txt "screentest: process after 15 s (a number means it is running):"
Status >>RAM:trialb-console.txt COMMAND=ScreenTest
Status >NIL: COMMAND=ScreenTest
If NOT WARN
  Break >NIL: `Status COMMAND=ScreenTest` C
EndIf
Wait 4
Echo >>RAM:trialb-console.txt "screentest: after Ctrl-C (empty means it closed):"
Status >>RAM:trialb-console.txt COMMAND=ScreenTest
CD SYS:

Echo >>RAM:trialb-console.txt "*N==== untangle ===="
Date >>RAM:trialb-console.txt
CD SYS:PkgV01/untangle
